From: Toemmsen96 <147745097+Toemmsen96@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd-common: handle alerts from the device without a regmap

wcd938x (and wcd937x/wcd939x) create the regmap on the TX SoundWire device
only, while both devices share the interrupt domain. An alert on the RX
device reached wcd_interrupt_callback() with dev_get_regmap() returning
NULL, and regmap_read(NULL) oopsed in the SoundWire IRQ thread, which then
exited with the IRQ still active (seen on a Xiaomi 12 when a phone call
started). Run the nested handler once in that case; it reads the status
through the codec's own regmap.
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-common.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-common.c
@@ -128,6 +128,19 @@
 	struct regmap *regmap = dev_get_regmap(&slave->dev, NULL);
 	u32 sts1, sts2, sts3;
 
+	/*
+	 * The codecs register their regmap on the TX SoundWire device only,
+	 * but the RX device shares the interrupt domain and can alert too.
+	 * The nested handler reads the status through the codec's own
+	 * regmap; without one here, run it once instead of polling a NULL
+	 * regmap (which oopsed in the IRQ thread on SM8450 when a call
+	 * started and left the codec without interrupts).
+	 */
+	if (!regmap) {
+		handle_nested_irq(irq_find_mapping(slave_irq, 0));
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+	}
+
 	do {
 		handle_nested_irq(irq_find_mapping(slave_irq, 0));
 		regmap_read(regmap, wcd_intr_status0, &sts1);
